# Netlify edge rules. No build step — Netlify reads this file directly.
#
# The repo root IS the publish directory, so every committed file is served.
# Non-public portal source (schema.sql, the SQL test harness) therefore does NOT
# live in this repo at all — it is in Hubspot/portal_seed/db/, outside the
# publish directory.
#
# That is deliberate rather than belt-and-braces: Netlify's `*` is a trailing
# splat, not a filename glob, so a rule like `/portal/*.sql` does NOT match and
# would have served the schema while looking like it was blocked. Keeping the
# files out of the directory is the only guarantee that does not depend on
# redirect semantics.
#
# portal/ now contains only what the browser is meant to fetch: the five pages,
# portal.css and portal.js.
